[{"id":"MuU_1.1.1","ref":"1.1.1","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 1","sa":["ॐ ब्रह्मा देवानां प्रथमः संबभूव विश्वस्य कर्ता","भुवनस्य गोप्ता । स ब्रह्मविद्यां सर्वविद्याप्रतिष्ठामथर्वाय","ज्येष्ठपुत्राय प्राह ॥ १॥"],"iast":["oṃ brahmā devānāṃ prathamaḥ saṃbabhūva viśvasya kartā","bhuvanasya goptā । sa brahmavidyāṃ sarvavidyāpratiṣṭhāmatharvāya","jyeṣṭhaputrāya prāha ॥ 1॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Brahma first of the Gods was born, the creator of all, the world’s protector; he to Atharvan, his eldest son, declared the God-knowledge in which all sciences have their foundation.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 131","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["ब्रह्मा","brahmā","Brahmā, the creator","brahman"],["देवानाम्","devānām","of the gods","deva"],["प्रथमः","prathamaḥ","first","prathama"],["संबभूव","saṃbabhūva","came into being","sambhū"],["विश्वस्य","viśvasya","of the universe","viśva"],["कर्ता","kartā","creator","kartṛ"],["भुवनस्य","bhuvanasya","of the world","bhuvana"],["गोप्ता","goptā","protector","goptṛ"],["स","sa","he","tad"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["विद्याम्","vidyām","knowledge (accusative)","vidyā"],["सर्व","sarva","all (compound member)","sarva"],["विद्या","vidyā","knowledge (compound member)","vidyā"],["प्रतिष्ठाम्","pratiṣṭhām","foundation","pratiṣṭhā"],["अथर्वाय","atharvāya","to Atharvan","atharva"],["ज्येष्ठ","jyeṣṭha","eldest (compound member)","jyeṣṭha"],["पुत्राय","putrāya","to the son","putra"],["प्राह","prāha","declared","prāh"]],"tr":{"text":"Om ! Brahma, the creator of the Universe and the protector of the world, was the first among the gods to manifest Himself. To His eldest son Atharva He imparted that knowledge of Brahman that is the basis of all knowledge.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.1.1.mp3","whole":[10.21,30.72]},"hasBhashya":false,"order":2,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.1.2","ref":"1.1.2","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 1","sa":["अथर्वणे यां प्रवदेत ब्रह्माऽथर्वा तं","पुरोवाचाङ्गिरे ब्रह्मविद्याम् ।","स भारद्वाजाय सत्यवाहाय प्राह","भारद्वाजोऽङ्गिरसे परावराम् ॥ २॥"],"iast":["atharvaṇe yāṃ pravadeta brahmā’tharvā taṃ","purovācāṅgire brahmavidyām ।","sa bhāradvājāya satyavāhāya prāha","bhāradvājo’ṅgirase parāvarām ॥ 2॥"],"alt":[{"text":"The God-knowledge by Brahma declared to Atharvan, Atharvan of old declared to Angir; he to Satyavaha the Bharadwaja told it, the Bharadwaja to Angiras, both the higher and the lower knowledge.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 131","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["अथर्वणे","atharvaṇe","to Atharvan","atharvaṇe"],["याम्","yām","which (knowledge)","yām"],["प्रवदेत","pravadeta","declared","pravadeta"],["ब्रह्मा","brahmā","Brahmā, the creator","brahmā"],["अथर्वा","atharvā","Atharvan","atharvā"],["तम्","tam","that","tam"],["पुरा","purā","of old","purā"],["उवाच","uvāca","declared","√vac"],["अङ्गिरे","aṅgire","to Aṅgir","aṅgire"],["ब्रह्मविद्याम्","brahmavidyām","knowledge of Brahman","brahmavidyām"],["स","sa","he","tad"],["भारद्वाजाय","bhāradvājāya","to Bhāradvāja","bhāradvāja"],["सत्यवाहाय","satyavāhāya","to Satyavāha","satyavāhāya"],["प्राह","prāha","declared","prāh"],["भारद्वाजः","bhāradvājaḥ","Bhāradvāja","bhāradvāja"],["अङ्गिरसे","aṅgirase","to Aṅgiras","aṅgiras"],["परावराम्","parāvarām","higher and lower (feminine accusative)","parāvara"]],"tr":{"text":"The Knowledge of Brahman that Brahma imparted to Atharva, Atharva transmitted to Angir in days of yore. He (Angir) passed it on to Satyavaha of the line of Bharadvaja. He of the line of Bharadvaja handed down to Angiras this knowledge that had been received in succession from the higher by the lower ones.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.1.2.mp3","whole":[32.76,55.18]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":3,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.1.3","ref":"1.1.3","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 1","sa":["शौनको ह वै महाशालोऽङ्गिरसं विधिवदुपसन्नः पप्रच्छ ।","कस्मिन्नु भगवो विज्ञाते सर्वमिदं विज्ञातं भवतीति ॥ ३॥"],"iast":["śaunako ha vai mahāśālo’ṅgirasaṃ vidhivadupasannaḥ papraccha ।","kasminnu bhagavo vijñāte sarvamidaṃ vijñātaṃ bhavatīti ॥ 3॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Shaunaka, the great house-lord, came to Angiras in the due way of the disciple and asked of him, “Lord, by knowing what does all this that is become known?”","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 131","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["शौनकः","śaunakaḥ","Shaunaka","śaunaka"],["ह","ha","indeed","ha"],["वै","vai","indeed","vai"],["महाशालः","mahāśālaḥ","great house-lord","mahāśāla"],["अङ्गिरसम्","aṅgirasam","Aṅgiras, the teacher","aṅgiras"],["विधिवत्","vidhivat","according to the due way","vidhivat"],["उपसन्नः","upasannaḥ","having approached","upasad"],["पप्रच्छ","papraccha","asked","pracch"],["कस्मिन्","kasmin","in what","ka"],["नु","nu","indeed","nu"],["भगवः","bhagavaḥ","O Lord","bhagavat"],["विज्ञाते","vijñāte","known","vijñā"],["सर्वम्","sarvam","all","sarva"],["इदम्","idam","this","idam"],["विज्ञातम्","vijñātam","known","vijñā"],["भवति","bhavati","becomes","bhū"],["इति","iti","thus","iti"]],"tr":{"text":"Saunaka, well known as a great householder, having approached Angiras duly, asked, ‘O adorable sir, (which is that thing) which having been known, all this becomes known ?’","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.1.3.mp3","whole":[56.1,74.65]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":4,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.1.4","ref":"1.1.4","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 1","sa":["तस्मै स होवाच ।","द्वे विद्ये वेदितव्ये इति ह स्म","यद्ब्रह्मविदो वदन्ति परा चैवापरा च ॥ ४॥"],"iast":["tasmai sa hovāca ।","dve vidye veditavye iti ha sma","yadbrahmavido vadanti parā caivāparā ca ॥ 4॥"],"alt":[{"text":"To him thus spoke Angiras: Twofold is the knowledge that must be known of which the knowers of the Brahman tell, the higher and the lower knowledge.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 131","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["तस्मै","tasmai","to that","tad"],["स","sa","he","tad"],["ह","ha","indeed","ha"],["उवाच","uvāca","said","vac"],["द्वे","dve","two","dvi"],["विद्ये","vidye","two kinds of knowledge","vidyā"],["वेदितव्ये","veditavye","to be known","vid"],["इति","iti","thus","iti"],["ह","ha","indeed","ha"],["स्म","sma","verily","sma"],["यत्","yat","which","yad"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["विदः","vidaḥ","knowers (in brahma-vidaḥ, knowers of Brahman)","vid"],["वदन्ति","vadanti","they say","vad"],["परा","parā","higher","para"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"],["अपरा","aparā","lower","apara"],["च","ca","and","ca"]],"tr":{"text":"To him he said, ‘\"There are two kinds of knowledge to be acquired – the higher and the lower\"; this is what, as tradition runs, the knowers of the import of the Vedas say.’","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.1.4.mp3","whole":[75.86,90.57]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":5,"up":"mundaka","takeaway":"There are two kinds of knowing: knowing about things, and knowing what makes knowing possible. Both matter; only one frees."},{"id":"MuU_1.1.5","ref":"1.1.5","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 1","sa":["तत्रापरा ऋग्वेदो यजुर्वेदः सामवेदोऽथर्ववेदः","शिक्षा कल्पो व्याकरणं निरुक्तं छन्दो ज्योतिषमिति ।","अथ परा यया तदक्षरमधिगम्यते ॥ ५॥"],"iast":["tatrāparā ṛgvedo yajurvedaḥ sāmavedo’tharvavedaḥ","śikṣā kalpo vyākaraṇaṃ niruktaṃ chando jyotiṣamiti ।","atha parā yayā tadakṣaramadhigamyate ॥ 5॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Of which the lower, the Rig Veda and the Yajur Veda and the Sama Veda and the Atharva Veda, chanting, ritual, grammar, etymological interpretation, and prosody and astronomy. And then the higher by which is known the Immutable.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 132","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["तत्र","tatra","there","tatra"],["अपरा","aparā","lower","apara"],["ऋग्वेदः","ṛgvedaḥ","Rigveda","ṛgveda"],["यजुर्वेदः","yajurvedaḥ","Yajurveda","yajurveda"],["सामवेदः","sāmavedaḥ","Samaveda","sāmaveda"],["अथर्ववेदः","atharvavedaḥ","Atharvaveda","atharvaveda"],["शिक्षा","śikṣā","phonetics","śikṣā"],["कल्पः","kalpaḥ","rituals","kalpa"],["व्याकरणम्","vyākaraṇam","grammar","vyākaraṇa"],["निरुक्तम्","niruktam","etymology","nirukta"],["छन्दः","chandaḥ","meter","chandas"],["ज्योतिषम्","jyotiṣam","astrology","jyotiṣa"],["इति","iti","thus","iti"],["अथ","atha","then","atha"],["परा","parā","higher","para"],["यया","yayā","by which (feminine)","yad"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["अक्षरम्","akṣaram","the imperishable","akṣara"],["अधिगम्यते","adhigamyate","is attained","adhigam"]],"tr":{"text":"Of these, the lower comprises the Rig-Veda, Yajur-Veda, Sama-Veda, Atharva-Veda, the science of pronunciation etc., the code of rituals, grammar, etymology, metre and astrology. Then there is the higher (knowledge) by which is attained that Imperishable.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.1.5.mp3","whole":[92.15,114.45]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":6,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.1.6","ref":"1.1.6","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 1","sa":["यत्तदद्रेश्यमग्राह्यमगोत्रमवर्णमचक्षुःश्रोत्रं तदपाणिपादम् ।","नित्यं विभुं सर्वगतं सुसूक्ष्मं","तदव्ययं यद्भूतयोनिं परिपश्यन्ति धीराः ॥ ६॥"],"iast":["yattadadreśyamagrāhyamagotramavarṇamacakṣuḥśrotraṃ tadapāṇipādam ।","nityaṃ vibhuṃ sarvagataṃ susūkṣmaṃ","tadavyayaṃ yadbhūtayoniṃ paripaśyanti dhīrāḥ ॥ 6॥"],"alt":[{"text":"That the invisible, that the unseizable, without connections, without hue, without eye or ear, that which is without hands or feet, eternal, pervading, which is in all things and impalpable, that which is Imperishable, that which is the womb of creatures sages behold everywhere.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 132","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["यत्","yat","which","yad"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["अद्रेश्यम्","adreśyam","invisible","adreśya"],["अग्राह्यम्","agrāhyam","ungraspable","agrāhya"],["अ","a","not","a"],["गोत्रम्","gotram","lineage (in a-gotram, without lineage)","gotra"],["अवर्णम्","avarṇam","without color","avarṇa"],["अ","a","not","a"],["चक्षुः","cakṣuḥ","eye","cakṣus"],["श्रोत्रम्","śrotram","hearing","śrotra"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["अ","a","not","a"],["पाणि","pāṇi","hand (in a-pāṇi-pādam, without hands or feet)","pāṇi"],["पादम्","pādam","foot (in a-pāṇi-pādam)","pāda"],["नित्यम्","nityam","eternal","nitya"],["विभुम्","vibhum","all-pervading","vibhu"],["सर्व","sarva","all (compound member)","sarva"],["गतम्","gatam","gone","gam"],["सु","su","well","su"],["सूक्ष्मम्","sūkṣmam","subtle (su-sūkṣmam, exceedingly subtle)","sūkṣma"],["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["अव्ययम्","avyayam","imperishable","avyaya"],["यत्","yat","which","yad"],["भूत","bhūta","being (compound member)","bhūta"],["योनिम्","yonim","source","yoni"],["परिपश्यन्ति","paripaśyanti","they behold","paripaś"],["धीराः","dhīrāḥ","the discerning","dhīra"]],"tr":{"text":"(By the higher knowledge) the wise realize everywhere that which cannot be perceived and grasped, which is without source, features, eyes, and ears, which has neither hands nor feet, which is eternal, multiformed, all-pervasive, extremely subtle, and undiminishing and which is the source of all.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.1.6.mp3","whole":[115.49,138.46]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":7,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.1.7","ref":"1.1.7","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 1","sa":["यथोर्णनाभिः सृजते गृह्णते च","यथा पृथिव्यामोषधयः संभवन्ति ।","यथा सतः पुरुषात्केशलोमानि","तथाऽक्षरात्संभवतीह विश्वम् ॥ ७॥"],"iast":["yathorṇanābhiḥ sṛjate gṛhṇate ca","yathā pṛthivyāmoṣadhayaḥ saṃbhavanti ।","yathā sataḥ puruṣātkeśalomāni","tathā’kṣarātsaṃbhavatīha viśvam ॥ 7॥"],"alt":[{"text":"As the spider puts out and gathers in, as herbs spring up upon the earth, as hair of head and body grow from a living man, so here all is born from the Immutable.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 132","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["यथा","yathā","as","yathā"],["ऊर्णनाभिः","ūrṇanābhiḥ","the spider","ūrṇanābhi"],["सृजते","sṛjate","creates, emits","sṛj"],["गृह्णते","gṛhṇate","retracts, takes back","grah"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["यथा","yathā","as","yathā"],["पृथिव्याम्","pṛthivyām","on the earth","pṛthivī"],["ओषधयः","oṣadhayaḥ","plants","oṣadhi"],["सम्भवन्ति","sambhavanti","arise","sambhū"],["यथा","yathā","as","yathā"],["सतः","sataḥ","from the existent, from a being","as"],["पुरुषात्","puruṣāt","from the Person","puruṣa"],["केश","keśa","hair of the head (compound member)","keśa"],["लोमानि","lomāni","body hairs","loman"],["तथा","tathā","thus","tathā"],["अक्षरात्","akṣarāt","from the imperishable","akṣara"],["सम्भवति","sambhavati","arises","sambhū"],["इह","iha","here","iha"],["विश्वम्","viśvam","all","viśva"]],"tr":{"text":"As a spider spreads out and withdraws (its thread), as on the earth grow the herbs (and trees), and as from a living man issues out hair (on the head and body), so out of the Imperishable does the Universe emerge here (in this phenomenal creation).","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.1.7.mp3","whole":[140.38,161.34]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":8,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.1.8","ref":"1.1.8","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 1","sa":["तपसा चीयते ब्रह्म ततोऽन्नमभिजायते ।","अन्नात्प्राणो मनः सत्यं लोकाः कर्मसु चामृतम् ॥ ८॥"],"iast":["tapasā cīyate brahma tato’nnamabhijāyate ।","annātprāṇo manaḥ satyaṃ lokāḥ karmasu cāmṛtam ॥ 8॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Brahman grows by his energy at work, and then from Him is Matter born, and out of Matter life, and mind and truth and the worlds, and in works immortality.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 132","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["तपसा","tapasā","through austerity","tapas"],["चीयते","cīyate","increases, accumulates","ci"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["ततस्","tatas","then","tatas"],["अन्नम्","annam","food","anna"],["अभिजायते","abhijāyate","is produced","abhijan"],["अन्नात्","annāt","from food","anna"],["प्राणः","prāṇaḥ","life-breath","prāṇa"],["मनः","manaḥ","mind","manas"],["सत्यम्","satyam","truth","satya"],["लोकाः","lokāḥ","worlds","loka"],["कर्मसु","karmasu","in works","karman"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["अमृतम्","amṛtam","immortality","amṛta"]],"tr":{"text":"Through knowledge Brahman increases in size. From that is born food (the Unmanifested). From food evolves Prana (Hiranyagarbha); (thence the cosmic) mind; (thence) the five elements; (thence) the worlds; (thence) the immortality that is in karmas.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.1.8.mp3","whole":[162.51,178.1]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":9,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.1.9","ref":"1.1.9","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 1","sa":["यः सर्वज्ञः सर्वविद्यस्य ज्ञानमयं तपः ।","तस्मादेतद्ब्रह्म नाम रूपमन्नं च जायते ॥ ९॥"],"iast":["yaḥ sarvajñaḥ sarvavidyasya jñānamayaṃ tapaḥ ।","tasmādetadbrahma nāma rūpamannaṃ ca jāyate ॥ 9॥"],"alt":[{"text":"He who is the Omniscient, the all-wise, He whose energy is all made of knowledge, from Him is born this that is Brahman here, this Name and Form and Matter.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 132","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["यः","yaḥ","who","yad"],["सर्व","sarva","all (compound member)","sarva"],["ज्ञः","jñaḥ","knowing","jña"],["सर्व","sarva","all (compound member)","sarva"],["विद्","vid","knowing (sarva-vid, all-knowing)","vid"],["यस्य","yasya","of which","yad"],["ज्ञान","jñāna","knowledge (compound member)","jñāna"],["मयम्","mayam","consisting of","maya"],["तपः","tapaḥ","self-discipline","tapas"],["तस्मात्","tasmāt","from that","tad"],["एतत्","etat","this","etad"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["नाम","nāma","name","nāma"],["रूपम्","rūpam","form","rūpa"],["अन्नम्","annam","food","anna"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["जायते","jāyate","is born","jan"]],"tr":{"text":"From Him, who is omniscient in general and all-knowing in detail and whose austerity is constituted by knowledge, evolve this (derivative) Brahman, name, colour and food.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.1.9.mp3","whole":[179.56,194.35]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":10,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.2.1","ref":"1.2.1","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 2","sa":["तदेतत्सत्यं मन्त्रेषु कर्माणि कवयो","यान्यपश्यंस्तानि त्रेतायां बहुधा संततानि ।","तान्याचरथ नियतं सत्यकामा एष वः","पन्थाः सुकृतस्य लोके ॥ १॥"],"iast":["tadetatsatyaṃ mantreṣu karmāṇi kavayo","yānyapaśyaṃstāni tretāyāṃ bahudhā saṃtatāni ।","tānyācaratha niyataṃ satyakāmā eṣa vaḥ","panthāḥ sukṛtasya loke ॥ 1॥"],"alt":[{"text":"This is That, the Truth of things: works which the sages beheld in the Mantras were in the Treta manifoldly extended. Works do ye perform religiously with one passion for the Truth; this is your road to the heaven of good deeds.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 133","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["तत्","tat","that","tad"],["एतत्","etat","this","etad"],["सत्यम्","satyam","truth","satya"],["मन्त्रेषु","mantreṣu","in the mantras","mantra"],["कर्माणि","karmāṇi","works","karman"],["कवयः","kavayaḥ","seers, wise ones","kavi"],["यानि","yāni","which","yad"],["अपश्यन्","apaśyan","they saw","paś"],["तानि","tāni","those","tad"],["त्रेतायाम्","tretāyām","in the Treta Yuga","tretā"],["बहुधा","bahudhā","in many ways","bahudhā"],["संततानि","saṃtatāni","extended","saṃtan"],["तानि","tāni","those","tad"],["आचरथ","ācaratha","perform","ācar"],["नियतम्","niyatam","with discipline, regularly","niyatam"],["सत्य","satya","truth (in satya-kāmāḥ)","satya"],["कामाः","kāmāḥ","desiring (satya-kāmāḥ, seekers of truth)","kāma"],["एष","eṣa","this (masculine)","etad"],["वः","vaḥ","for you","tvad"],["पन्थाः","panthāḥ","path","pathin"],["सुकृतस्य","sukṛtasya","of virtue","sukṛta"],["लोके","loke","in the world","loka"]],"tr":{"text":"That thing that is such, is true. The karmas that the wise discovered in the mantras are accomplished variously (in the context of the sacrifice) where the three Vedic duties get united. You perform them for ever with desire for the true results. This is your path leading to the fruits of karma acquired by yourselves.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.2.1.mp3","whole":[197.23,219.65]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":11,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.2.2","ref":"1.2.2","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 2","sa":["यदा लेलायते ह्यर्चिः समिद्धे हव्यवाहने ।","तदाऽऽज्यभागावन्तरेणाऽऽहुतीः प्रतिपादयेच्छ्रद्धया हुतम् ॥ २॥"],"iast":["yadā lelāyate hyarciḥ samiddhe havyavāhane ।","tadā’’jyabhāgāvantareṇā’’hutīḥ pratipādayecchraddhayā hutam ॥ 2॥"],"alt":[{"text":"When the fire of the sacrifice is kindled and the flame sways and quivers, then between the double pourings of butter cast therein with faith thy offerings.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 133","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["यदा","yadā","when","yadā"],["लेलायते","lelāyate","flickers","lelāy"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["अर्चिः","arciḥ","flame","arcis"],["समिद्धे","samiddhe","when kindled","samindh"],["हव्यवाहने","havyavāhane","in the bearer of offerings, the fire","havyavāhana"],["तदा","tadā","then","tadā"],["आज्यभागौ","ājyabhāgau","the two portions of clarified butter","ājyabhāga"],["अन्तरेण","antareṇa","between","antareṇa"],["आहुतीः","āhutīḥ","oblations","āhuti"],["प्रतिपादयेत्","pratipādayet","one should offer","pratipāday"],["श्रद्धया","śraddhayā","with faith","śraddhā"],["हुतम्","hutam","offered in sacrifice","hu"]],"tr":{"text":"When, the fire being set ablaze, the flame shoots up, one should offer the oblations into that part that is in between the right and the left.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.2.2.mp3","whole":[223.86,240.03]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":12,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.2.3","ref":"1.2.3","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 2","sa":["यस्याग्निहोत्रमदर्शमपौर्णमासमचातुर्मास्यमनाग्रयणमतिथिवर्जितं च ।","अहुतमवैश्वदेवमविधिना हुतमासप्तमांस्तस्य लोकान् हिनस्ति ॥ ३॥"],"iast":["yasyāgnihotramadarśamapaurṇamāsamacāturmāsyamanāgrayaṇamatithivarjitaṃ ca ।","ahutamavaiśvadevamavidhinā hutamāsaptamāṃstasya lokān hinasti ॥ 3॥"],"alt":[{"text":"For he whose altar-fires are empty of the new-moon offering and the full-moon offering and the offering of the rains and the offering of the first fruits, or unfed, or fed without right ritual, or without guests or without the dues to the Vishwa-Devas, destroys his hope of all the seven worlds.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 133","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["यस्य","yasya","of which","yad"],["अग्निहोत्रम्","agnihotram","the Agnihotra fire offering","agnihotra"],["अ","a","not","a"],["दर्शम्","darśam","new-moon rite (a-darśam: lacking it)","darśa"],["अ","a","not","a"],["पौर्णमासम्","paurṇamāsam","full-moon rite (a-paurṇamāsam: lacking it)","paurṇamāsa"],["अ","a","not","a"],["चातुर्मास्यम्","cāturmāsyam","four-monthly seasonal rite (a-cāturmāsyam: lacking it)","cāturmāsya"],["अन्","an","not","an"],["आग्रयणम्","āgrayaṇam","first-fruits offering (an-āgrayaṇam: lacking it)","āgrayaṇa"],["अतिथि","atithi","guest (compound member)","atithi"],["वर्जितम्","varjitam","deprived of","varjay"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["अ","a","not","a"],["हुतम्","hutam","offered in sacrifice","hu"],["अ","a","not","a"],["वैश्वदेवम्","vaiśvadevam","offering to all the gods (a-vaiśvadevam: lacking it)","vaiśvadeva"],["अविधिना","avidhinā","contrary to the prescribed rule","avidhi"],["हुतम्","hutam","offered in sacrifice","hu"],["आ","ā","up to","ā"],["सप्तमान्","saptamān","the seventh (worlds","saptama"],["तस्य","tasya","of that","tad"],["लोकान्","lokān","worlds","loka"],["हिनस्ति","hinasti","injures","hiṃs"]],"tr":{"text":"It (i.e. the Agnihotra) destroys the seven worlds of that man whose Agnihotra (sacrifice) is without Darsa and Paurnamasa (rites), devoid of Chaturmasya, bereft of Agrayana, unblest with guests, goes unperformed, is unaccompanied by Vaisvadeva (rite) and is performed perfunctorily.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.2.3.mp3","whole":[240.03,263.87]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":13,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.2.4","ref":"1.2.4","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 2","sa":["काली कराली च मनोजवा च","सुलोहिता या च सुधूम्रवर्णा ।","स्फुलिङ्गिनी विश्वरुची च देवी","लेलायमाना इति सप्त जिह्वाः ॥ ४॥"],"iast":["kālī karālī ca manojavā ca","sulohitā yā ca sudhūmravarṇā ।","sphuliṅginī viśvarucī ca devī","lelāyamānā iti sapta jihvāḥ ॥ 4॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Kali, the black, Karali, the terrible, Manojava, thoughtswift, Sulohita, blood-red, Sudhumravarna, smoke-hued, Sphulingini, scattering sparks, Vishwaruchi, the all-beautiful, these are the seven swaying tongues of the fire.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 133","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["काली","kālī","the Black one, a tongue of flame","kālī"],["कराली","karālī","the Terrible one","karālī"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["मनोजवा","manojavā","Swift as Thought","manojavā"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["सुलोहिता","sulohitā","Very Red","sulohitā"],["या","yā","which","yad"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["सुधूम्रवर्णा","sudhūmravarṇā","Deep Smoke-coloured","sudhūmravarṇā"],["स्फुलिङ्गिनी","sphuliṅginī","Spark-scattering","sphuliṅginī"],["विश्वरुची","viśvarucī","All-shining","viśvarucī"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["देवी","devī","divine","devī"],["लेलायमाना","lelāyamānā","flickering","lelāyamānā"],["इति","iti","thus","iti"],["सप्त","sapta","seven","saptan"],["जिह्वाः","jihvāḥ","tongues","jihvā"]],"tr":{"text":"Kali, Karali, Manojava and Sulohita and that which is Sudhumravarna, as also Sphulingini, and the shining Visvaruchi – these are the seven flaming tongues.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.2.4.mp3","whole":[265.08,284.13]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":14,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.2.5","ref":"1.2.5","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 2","sa":["एतेषु यश्चरते भ्राजमानेषु यथाकालं","चाहुतयो ह्याददायन् ।","तं नयन्त्येताः सूर्यस्य रश्मयो यत्र","देवानां पतिरेकोऽधिवासः ॥ ५॥"],"iast":["eteṣu yaścarate bhrājamāneṣu yathākālaṃ","cāhutayo hyādadāyan ।","taṃ nayantyetāḥ sūryasya raśmayo yatra","devānāṃ patireko’dhivāsaḥ ॥ 5॥"],"alt":[{"text":"He who in these when they are blazing bright performs the rites, in their due season, him his fires of sacrifice take and they lead him, these rays of the Sun, there where the Overlord of the gods is the Inhabitant on high.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 134","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["एतेषु","eteṣu","in these","etad"],["यः","yaḥ","who","yad"],["चरते","carate","performs the rite","car"],["भ्राजमानेषु","bhrājamāneṣu","while blazing","bhrāj"],["यथाकालम्","yathākālam","at the proper time","yathākālam"],["च","ca","and","ca"],["आहुतयः","āhutayaḥ","oblations","āhuti"],["तम्","tam","him","tad"],["नयन्ति","nayanti","lead","nī"],["एताः","etāḥ","these (oblations)","etad"],["सूर्यस्य","sūryasya","of the sun","sūrya"],["रश्मयः","raśmayaḥ","rays","raśmi"],["यत्र","yatra","where","yatra"],["देवानाम्","devānām","of the gods","deva"],["पतिः","patiḥ","lord","pati"],["एकः","ekaḥ","one","eka"],["अधिवासः","adhivāsaḥ","abode","adhivāsa"]],"tr":{"text":"These oblations turn into the rays of the sun and taking him up they lead him, who performs the rites in these shining flames at the proper time, to where the single lord of the gods presides over all.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.2.5.mp3","whole":[284.88,306.84]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":15,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.2.6","ref":"1.2.6","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 2","sa":["एह्येहीति तमाहुतयः सुवर्चसः","सूर्यस्य रश्मिभिर्यजमानं वहन्ति ।","प्रियां वाचमभिवदन्त्योऽर्चयन्त्य","एष वः पुण्यः सुकृतो ब्रह्मलोकः ॥ ६॥"],"iast":["ehyehīti tamāhutayaḥ suvarcasaḥ","sūryasya raśmibhiryajamānaṃ vahanti ।","priyāṃ vācamabhivadantyo’rcayantya","eṣa vaḥ puṇyaḥ sukṛto brahmalokaḥ ॥ 6॥"],"alt":[{"text":"“Come with us”, “Come with us”, they cry to him, these luminous fires of sacrifice, and they bear him by the rays of the Sun speaking to him pleasant words of sweetness, doing him homage, “This is your holy world of Brahman and the heaven of your righteousness.”","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 134","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["एहि","ehi","come!","e"],["एहि","ehi","come!","e"],["इति","iti","thus","iti"],["तम्","tam","him","tad"],["आहुतयः","āhutayaḥ","oblations","āhuti"],["सु","su","well","su"],["वर्चसः","varcasaḥ","lustre (su-varcasaḥ, of goodly splendour)","varcas"],["सूर्यस्य","sūryasya","of the sun","sūrya"],["रश्मिभिः","raśmibhiḥ","by the rays","raśmi"],["यजमानम्","yajamānam","the sacrificer","yaj"],["वहन्ति","vahanti","carry","vah"],["प्रियाम्","priyām","pleasing","priya"],["वाचम्","vācam","speech","vāc"],["अभिवदन्त्यः","abhivadantyaḥ","speaking to him","abhivad"],["अर्चयन्त्यः","arcayantyaḥ","honouring","arcay"],["एष","eṣa","this (masculine)","etad"],["वः","vaḥ","for you","tvad"],["पुण्यः","puṇyaḥ","holy","puṇya"],["सु","su","well","su"],["कृतः","kṛtaḥ","made","kṛt"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["लोकः","lokaḥ","world","loka"]],"tr":{"text":"Saying, ‘Come, come’, uttering pleasing words such as, ‘This is your well-earned, virtuous path which leads to heaven’, and offering him adoration, the scintillating oblations carry the sacrificer along the rays of the sun.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.2.6.mp3","whole":[307.93,330.52]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":16,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.2.7","ref":"1.2.7","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 2","sa":["प्लवा ह्येते अदृढा यज्ञरूपा","अष्टादशोक्तमवरं येषु कर्म ।","एतच्छ्रेयो येऽभिनन्दन्ति मूढा","जरामृत्युं ते पुनरेवापि यन्ति ॥ ७॥"],"iast":["plavā hyete adṛḍhā yajñarūpā","aṣṭādaśoktamavaraṃ yeṣu karma ।","etacchreyo ye’bhinandanti mūḍhā","jarāmṛtyuṃ te punarevāpi yanti ॥ 7॥"],"alt":[{"text":"But frail are the ships of sacrifice, frail these forms of sacrifice, all the eighteen of them, in which are declared the lower works; fools are they who hail them as the highest good and they come yet again to this world of age and death.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 134","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["प्लवाः","plavāḥ","rafts","plava"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["एते","ete","these","etad"],["अदृढाः","adṛḍhāḥ","insecure","adṛḍha"],["यज्ञ","yajña","sacrifice (compound member)","yajña"],["रूपाः","rūpāḥ","forms","rūpa"],["अष्टादश","aṣṭādaśa","eighteen","aṣṭādaśan"],["उक्तम्","uktam","declared","vac"],["अवरम्","avaram","lower","avara"],["येषु","yeṣu","in which","yad"],["कर्म","karma","work","karman"],["एतत्","etat","this","etad"],["श्रेयः","śreyaḥ","the better","śreyas"],["ये","ye","who","yad"],["अभिनन्दन्ति","abhinandanti","delight in","abhinand"],["मूढाः","mūḍhāḥ","deluded people","muh"],["जरा","jarā","old age (compound member)","jarā"],["मृत्युम्","mṛtyum","death","mṛtyu"],["ते","te","they","tad"],["पुनर्","punar","again","punar"],["एवा","evā","indeed","eva"],["अपियन्ति","apiyanti","go into","apī"]],"tr":{"text":"Since these eighteen constituents of a sacrifice, on whom the inferior karma has been said to rest, are perishable because of their fragility, therefore those ignorant people who get elated with the idea ‘This is (the cause of) bliss’, undergo old age and death over again.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.2.7.mp3","whole":[331.35,352.65]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":17,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.2.8","ref":"1.2.8","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 2","sa":["अविद्यायामन्तरे वर्तमानाः","स्वयं धीराः पण्डितंमन्यमानाः ।","जङ्घन्यमानाः परियन्ति मूढा","अन्धेनैव नीयमाना यथान्धाः ॥ ८॥"],"iast":["avidyāyāmantare vartamānāḥ","svayaṃ dhīrāḥ paṇḍitaṃmanyamānāḥ ।","jaṅghanyamānāḥ pariyanti mūḍhā","andhenaiva nīyamānā yathāndhāḥ ॥ 8॥"],"alt":[{"text":"They who dwell shut within the Ignorance and they hold themselves for learned men thinking “We, even we are the wise and the sages” — fools are they and they wander around beaten and stumbling like blind men led by the blind.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 134","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["अविद्यायाम्","avidyāyām","in ignorance","avidyā"],["अन्तरे","antare","in the midst","antara"],["वर्तमानाः","vartamānāḥ","existing","vṛt"],["स्वयम्","svayam","oneself","svayam"],["धीराः","dhīrāḥ","the discerning","dhīra"],["पण्डितम्","paṇḍitam","learned (in paṇḍitaṃ-manyamānāḥ)","paṇḍita"],["मन्यमानाः","manyamānāḥ","considering themselves","man"],["जङ्घन्यमानाः","jaṅghanyamānāḥ","being struck again and again","jaṅghan"],["परियन्ति","pariyanti","go round","parī"],["मूढाः","mūḍhāḥ","the deluded","muh"],["अन्धेन","andhena","by a blind person","andha"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"],["नीयमानाः","nīyamānāḥ","being led","nī"],["यथा","yathā","as","yathā"],["अन्धाः","andhāḥ","blind people","andha"]],"tr":{"text":"Remaining within the fold of ignorance and thinking, ‘We are ourselves wise and learned’, the fools, while being buffeted very much, ramble about like the blind led by the blind alone.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.2.8.mp3","whole":[355.19,378.74]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":18,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.2.9","ref":"1.2.9","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 2","sa":["अविद्यायां बहुधा वर्तमाना वयं","कृतार्था इत्यभिमन्यन्ति बालाः ।","यत्कर्मिणो न प्रवेदयन्ति रागात्तेनातुराः क्षीणलोकाश्च्यवन्ते ॥ ९॥"],"iast":["avidyāyāṃ bahudhā vartamānā vayaṃ","kṛtārthā ityabhimanyanti bālāḥ ।","yatkarmiṇo na pravedayanti rāgāttenāturāḥ kṣīṇalokāścyavante ॥ 9॥"],"alt":[{"text":"They dwell in many bonds of the Ignorance, children thinking, “We have achieved our aim of Paradise”; for when the men of works are held by their affections, and arrive not at the Knowledge, then they are overtaken by anguish, then their Paradise wastes by enjoying and they fall from their heavens.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, pp. 134, 135","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["अविद्यायाम्","avidyāyām","in ignorance","avidyā"],["बहुधा","bahudhā","in many ways","bahudhā"],["वर्तमानाः","vartamānāḥ","remaining","vṛt"],["वयम्","vayam","we","mad"],["कृतार्थाः","kṛtārthāḥ","having achieved the goal","kṛtārtha"],["इति","iti","thus","iti"],["अभिमन्यन्ति","abhimanyanti","imagine","abhiman"],["बालाः","bālāḥ","the immature","bāla"],["यत्","yat","which","yat"],["कर्मिणः","karmiṇaḥ","performers of ritual works","karmin"],["न","na","not","na"],["प्रवेदयन्ति","pravedayanti","understand","praveday"],["रागात्","rāgāt","because of attachment","rāga"],["तेन","tena","therefore","tena"],["आतुराः","āturāḥ","afflicted","ātura"],["क्षीण","kṣīṇa","exhausted (in kṣīṇa-lokāḥ, whose worlds are exhausted)","kṣi"],["लोकाः","lokāḥ","worlds","loka"],["च्यवन्ते","cyavante","fall away","cyu"]],"tr":{"text":"Continuing diversely in the midst of ignorance, the unenlightened take airs by thinking, ‘We have attained the goal.’ Since the men, engaged in karma, do not understand (the truth) under the influence of attachment, thereby they become afflicted with sorrow and are deprived of heaven on the exhaustion of the results of karma.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.2.9.mp3","whole":[380.03,403.12]},"hasBhashya":false,"order":19,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.2.10","ref":"1.2.10","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 2","sa":["इष्टापूर्तं मन्यमाना वरिष्ठं","नान्यच्छ्रेयो वेदयन्ते प्रमूढाः ।","नाकस्य पृष्ठे ते सुकृतेऽनुभूत्वेमं","लोकं हीनतरं वा विशन्ति ॥ १०॥"],"iast":["iṣṭāpūrtaṃ manyamānā variṣṭhaṃ","nānyacchreyo vedayante pramūḍhāḥ ।","nākasya pṛṣṭhe te sukṛte’nubhūtvemaṃ","lokaṃ hīnataraṃ vā viśanti ॥ 10॥"],"alt":[{"text":"Minds bewildered who hold the oblation offered and the well dug for the greatest righteousness and know not any other highest good, on the back of heaven they enjoy the world won by their righteousness and enter again this or even a lower world.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 135","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["इष्टापूर्तम्","iṣṭāpūrtam","sacrifice and charitable works","iṣṭāpūrta"],["मन्यमानाः","manyamānāḥ","considering","man"],["वरिष्ठम्","variṣṭham","the highest","variṣṭha"],["ना","nā","not","na"],["अन्यत्","anyat","anything else","anya"],["श्रेयः","śreyaḥ","a higher good","śreyas"],["वेदयन्ते","vedayante","know","veday"],["प्रमूढाः","pramūḍhāḥ","deeply deluded","pramuh"],["नाकस्य","nākasya","of heaven","nāka"],["पृष्ठे","pṛṣṭhe","on the summit","pṛṣṭha"],["ते","te","they","tad"],["सुकृते","sukṛte","in the well-won reward of good deeds","sukṛta"],["अनुभूत्वा","anubhūtvā","having experienced","anubhū"],["इमम्","imam","this","idam"],["लोकम्","lokam","world","loka"],["हीनतरम्","hīnataram","a lower one","hīnatara"],["वा","vā","or","vā"],["विशन्ति","viśanti","enter","viś"]],"tr":{"text":"The deluded fools, believing the rites inculcated by the Vedas and the Smritis to be the highest, do not understand the other thing (that leads to) liberation. They, having enjoyed (the fruits of actions) in the abode of pleasure on the heights of heaven, enter this world or an inferior one.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.2.10.mp3","whole":[406.5,429.34]},"hasBhashya":false,"order":20,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.2.11","ref":"1.2.11","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 2","sa":["तपःश्रद्धे ये ह्युपवसन्त्यरण्ये","शान्ता विद्वांसो भैक्ष्यचर्यां चरन्तः ।","सूर्यद्वारेण ते विरजाः प्रयान्ति","यत्रामृतः स पुरुषो ह्यव्ययात्मा ॥ ११॥"],"iast":["tapaḥśraddhe ye hyupavasantyaraṇye","śāntā vidvāṃso bhaikṣyacaryāṃ carantaḥ ।","sūryadvāreṇa te virajāḥ prayānti","yatrāmṛtaḥ sa puruṣo hyavyayātmā ॥ 11॥"],"alt":[{"text":"But they who in the forest follow after faith and selfdiscipline, calm and full of knowledge, living upon alms, cast from them the dust of their passions, and through the gate of the Sun they pass on there where is the Immortal, the Spirit, the Self undecaying and imperishable.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 135","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["तपः","tapaḥ","self-discipline","tapas"],["श्रद्धे","śraddhe","faith (in tapaḥ-śraddhe, austerity and faith)","śraddhā"],["ये","ye","who","yad"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["उपवसन्ति","upavasanti","dwell, live","upavas"],["अरण्ये","araṇye","in the forest","araṇya"],["शान्ताः","śāntāḥ","peaceful","śam"],["विद्वांसः","vidvāṃsaḥ","wise ones","vid"],["भैक्ष","bhaikṣa","alms (compound member)","bhaikṣa"],["चर्याम्","caryām","way of life","caryā"],["चरन्तः","carantaḥ","practicing, living","car"],["सूर्य","sūrya","sun (compound member)","sūrya"],["द्वारेण","dvāreṇa","through the gate","dvāra"],["ते","te","they","tad"],["विरजाः","virajāḥ","free from impurities","viraja"],["प्रयान्ति","prayānti","go, travel","prayā"],["यत्र","yatra","where","yatra"],["अमृतः","amṛtaḥ","immortal","amṛta"],["स","sa","he","tad"],["पुरुषः","puruṣaḥ","Person","puruṣa"],["हि","hi","for","hi"],["अव्यय","avyaya","imperishable (in avyayātmā)","avyaya"],["आत्मा","ātmā","Self","ātman"]],"tr":{"text":"Those who live in the forest, while begging for alms – viz. those (forest-dwellers and hermits) who resort to the duties of their respective stages of life as well as to meditation – and the learned (householders) who have their senses under control – (they) after becoming freed from dirt, go by the path of the sun to where lives that Purusha, immortal and undecaying by nature.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.2.11.mp3","whole":[430.72,454.64]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":21,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.2.12","ref":"1.2.12","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 2","sa":["परीक्ष्य लोकान् कर्मचितान् ब्राह्मणो","निर्वेदमायान्नास्त्यकृतः कृतेन ।","तद्विज्ञानार्थं स गुरुमेवाभिगच्छेत्","समित्पाणिः श्रोत्रियं ब्रह्मनिष्ठम् ॥ १२॥"],"iast":["parīkṣya lokān karmacitān brāhmaṇo","nirvedamāyānnāstyakṛtaḥ kṛtena ।","tadvijñānārthaṃ sa gurumevābhigacchet","samitpāṇiḥ śrotriyaṃ brahmaniṣṭham ॥ 12॥"],"alt":[{"text":"The seeker of the Brahman, having put to the test the worlds piled up by works, arrives at world-distaste, for not by work done is reached He who is Uncreated. For the knowledge of That, let him approach, fuel in hand, a Guru, one who is learned in the Veda and is devoted to contemplation of the Brahman.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 135","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["परीक्ष्य","parīkṣya","having examined","parīkṣ"],["लोकान्","lokān","worlds","loka"],["कर्म","karma","work","karman"],["चितान्","citān","accumulated","ci"],["ब्राह्मणः","brāhmaṇaḥ","a Brāhmaṇa","brāhmaṇa"],["निर्वेदम्","nirvedam","dispassion","nirveda"],["आयात्","āyāt","should develop","āyā"],["न","na","not","na"],["अस्ति","asti","is","as"],["अ","a","not","a"],["कृतः","kṛtaḥ","made (a-kṛtaḥ: the unmade)","kṛ"],["कृतेन","kṛtena","by the created","kṛ"],["तद्","tad","that (in tad-vijñāna-artham)","tad"],["विज्ञान","vijñāna","knowledge","vijñāna"],["अर्थम्","artham","for the purpose of","artha"],["स","sa","he","tad"],["गुरुम्","gurum","guru","guru"],["एव","eva","indeed","eva"],["अभिगच्छेत्","abhigacchet","should approach","abhigam"],["समिध्","samidh","fuel-stick (compound member)","samidh"],["पाणिः","pāṇiḥ","hand (samit-pāṇiḥ: with fuel-stick in hand)","pāṇi"],["श्रोत्रियम्","śrotriyam","learned in the Vedas","śrotriya"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["निष्ठम्","niṣṭham","firmly established (in Brahman)","niṣṭhā"]],"tr":{"text":"A Brahmana should resort to renunciation after examining the worlds acquired through karma, with the help of this maxim: ‘There is nothing (here) that is not the result of karma; so what is the need of (performing) karma ?’ For knowing that Reality he should go, with sacrificial faggots in hand, only to a teacher versed in the Vedas and absorbed in Brahman.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.2.12.mp3","whole":[454.64,478.52]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":22,"up":"mundaka"},{"id":"MuU_1.2.13","ref":"1.2.13","section":"Muṇḍaka 1 · Section 2","sa":["तस्मै स विद्वानुपसन्नाय सम्यक्","प्रशान्तचित्ताय शमान्विताय ।","येनाक्षरं पुरुषं वेद सत्यं प्रोवाच","तां तत्त्वतो ब्रह्मविद्याम् ॥ १३॥"],"iast":["tasmai sa vidvānupasannāya samyak","praśāntacittāya śamānvitāya ।","yenākṣaraṃ puruṣaṃ veda satyaṃ provāca","tāṃ tattvato brahmavidyām ॥ 13॥"],"alt":[{"text":"To him because he has taken entire refuge with him, with a heart tranquillised and a spirit at peace, that man of knowledge declares in its principles the science of the Brahman by which one comes to know the Immutable Spirit, the True and Real.","by":"Sri Aurobindo","cite":"Sri Aurobindo · CWSA 18, p. 136","source":"upanishads.org.in"}],"words":[["तस्मै","tasmai","to that","tad"],["स","sa","he","tad"],["विद्वान्","vidvān","one who knows","vid"],["उपसन्नाय","upasannāya","to the one who has approached","upasad"],["सम्यक्","samyak","properly","samyak"],["प्रशान्त","praśānta","tranquil","praśam"],["चित्ताय","cittāya","to one whose mind is (tranquil)","citta"],["शम","śama","calm","śama"],["अन्विताय","anvitāya","to one endowed with","anvita"],["येन","yena","by which","yad"],["अक्षरम्","akṣaram","the imperishable","akṣara"],["पुरुषम्","puruṣam","Person","puruṣa"],["वेद","veda","knows","vid"],["सत्यम्","satyam","truth","satya"],["प्रोवाच","provāca","imparted, said","pravac"],["ताम्","tām","her","tad"],["तत्त्वतः","tattvataḥ","in essence, truly","tattva"],["ब्रह्म","brahma","Brahman","brahman"],["विद्याम्","vidyām","knowledge (accusative)","vidyā"]],"tr":{"text":"To him who has approached duly, whose heart is calm and whose outer organs are under control, that man of enlightenment should adequately impart that knowledge of Brahman by which one realizes the true and imperishable Purusha.","by":"Swami Gambhirananda","source":"108 Upanishads (comp. R. Sheppard)"},"audio":{"mp3":"https://s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/upanishaddata/SplitAudio/mundakopanisad/4.1.2.13.mp3","whole":[480.94,501.61]},"hasBhashya":true,"order":23,"up":"mundaka"}]